      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: graduated licensing, license classes and renewal",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: graduated licensing, license classes and renewal\nAudience: Minnesota teens moving through graduated licensing and the parents or guardians who sign and log their practice hours, plus adult permit holders and current drivers checking renewal rules.\nWhy it matters to a first-timer: the permit eligibility rules [A01], the provisional license requirements and night limit [A02], and the passenger limits [A03] are the core teen-driver items on the written test.\nLevel: dense threshold recall (ages, months, hours, passenger counts, weights); high confusion risk because teen and adult rules differ by only a few numbers.\nPrerequisites: the first half of chapter one on eligibility and the three tests.\n",
